    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0134" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/131½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President
                        Roosevelt</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-08">March 8, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I am enclosing a
                    memorandum of a conversation I had with the British Ambassador yesterday
                    evening. I think that whatever misapprehension existed in the mind of Lord
                        Halifax<anchor n="21" xml:id="d80-f1"/> has now been cleared up as a result
                    of a cable which Sir Ronald said he would send him last night. In view of the
                    importance of the rest of the message, I thought you would probably want to read
                    this memorandum.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d80-a1.xml" xpointer="d80-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="21" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
                <p>Successor to Anthony Eden as British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs,
                    March 1, 1938.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
